=You are an email triage assistant for a SaaS support team. Classify the email below into EXACTLY one intent category: Question, Request, Complaint, FYI, or Spam. Also assign a priority (high, medium, or low) and write a one-sentence summary.

Respond with ONLY valid JSON — no markdown fences, no commentary — in exactly this shape:
{"classification": "<Question|Request|Complaint|FYI|Spam>", "priority": "<high|medium|low>", "summary": "<one sentence>"}

Definitions: Question = customer asks how to do something or whether something is possible. Request = customer asks you to take an action (upgrade, refund, provision, change). Complaint = customer is upset about a problem. FYI = informational only, no action needed. Spam = unsolicited junk/scam.

EMAIL
From: {{ $json.from }}
Subject: {{ $json.subject }}
Body:
{{ $json.body }}

IMPORTANT: Do not think out loud. Do not explain. Your ENTIRE response must be that single line of JSON and nothing else.

parameters.jsCode:
// Parse the model's verdict (handles raw JSON, fenced JSON, or reasoning text)
const raw = $json.content?.parts?.[0]?.text ?? '';
const cleaned = raw.replace(/```json/gi, '```').replace(/```/g, '').trim();
const allowed = ['Question', 'Request', 'Complaint', 'FYI', 'Spam'];
let verdict = null;
// 1) Try every {...} candidate, last one wins (models often restate the schema first)
const candidates = cleaned.match(/\{[^{}]*\}/g) ?? [];
for (const c of candidates.reverse()) {
  try {
    const p = JSON.parse(c);
    if (p && allowed.includes(p.classification)) { verdict = p; break; }
  } catch (e) { /* keep looking */ }
}
// 2) Fallback: scrape labeled lines from reasoning-style output (take LAST occurrence)
if (!verdict) {
  const grabAll = (re) => { let m, last = null; while ((m = re.exec(cleaned)) !== null) last = m[1]; return last; };
  const cls = grabAll(/classification[\s\"':*]*\s*(Question|Request|Complaint|FYI|Spam)/gi);
  const pri = grabAll(/priority[\s\"':*]*\s*(high|medium|low)/gi);
  const sum = grabAll(/summary[\s\"':*]*\s*([^\n\"]{10,300})/gi);
  verdict = { classification: cls, priority: (pri ?? 'medium').toLowerCase(), summary: (sum ?? '').trim() };
}
if (!allowed.includes(verdict.classification)) verdict.classification = 'FYI';
const email = $('Sample Inbox (Demo Data)').item.json;
return {
  json: {
    messageId: email.messageId,
    from: email.from,
    subject: email.subject,
    body: email.body,
    receivedAt: email.receivedAt,
    classification: verdict.classification,
    priority: verdict.priority ?? 'medium',
    summary: verdict.summary ?? ''
  }
};

values.content:
=You are a senior customer support agent at BrightLoop (a SaaS billing analytics product). Write a complete, warm, professional reply email (under 160 words) to the customer email below. Match the tone to the intent: apologize and de-escalate for complaints, answer clearly for questions, confirm next steps for requests. Sign as "Alex — BrightLoop Support". Wrap your final reply between the exact markers <<<REPLY>>> and <<<END>>>. Anything outside the markers is discarded, so the complete email MUST appear between them. Do not think out loud before the markers.

INTENT: {{ $json.classification }} (priority: {{ $json.priority }})
FROM: {{ $json.from }}
SUBJECT: {{ $json.subject }}
BODY:
{{ $json.body }}

IMPORTANT: Do not think out loud, do not plan, do not repeat these instructions. Start your response DIRECTLY with the greeting line (e.g. "Hi Rachel,") and output only the reply.

parameters.jsCode:
// Extract the final reply text from Gemini's output
const item = $json;
let rawDraft = '';
if (item.content && Array.isArray(item.content.parts)) {
  rawDraft = item.content.parts.filter(p => !p.thought).map(p => p.text || '').join('');
} else if (item.text) { rawDraft = item.text; }
rawDraft = (rawDraft || '').trim();
let draft = '';
const lastIdx = rawDraft.lastIndexOf('<<<REPLY>>>');
if (lastIdx !== -1) {
  draft = rawDraft.slice(lastIdx + 11);
  const endIdx = draft.indexOf('<<<END>>>');
  if (endIdx !== -1) draft = draft.slice(0, endIdx);
  draft = draft.trim();
}
if (draft.length < 40) {
  const g = /(Hi|Hello|Dear|Hey)\s+[A-Z][a-zA-Z]*,/g;
  let m, last = -1;
  while ((m = g.exec(rawDraft)) !== null) last = m.index;
  if (last !== -1) {
    draft = rawDraft.slice(last);
    const s = draft.indexOf('<<<END>>>');
    if (s !== -1) draft = draft.slice(0, s);
    draft = draft.trim();
  }
}
if (draft.length < 40) draft = rawDraft;
const email = $('Parse Classification').item.json;
return { json: { ...email, draftReply: draft } };

